course: dictionary
lesson: 11176
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Winner is one of them. It can mean a person, team or animal that wins. It can also mean something very successful or popular. The words around it tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «After the race, the winner was the girl with the smallest time.» The race and the smallest time are the clues. A winner is the one who covers the distance in the least time, so here winner means the person who wins the race.
explain: «This new recipe is a winner.» There is no person here, and no prize. Try swapping in another word: «This new recipe is a success.» It still makes sense, so winner means something very popular here.
explain: «A good winner is happy without rubbing it in, and a good loser congratulates the winner.» This sentence is about behaviour. A good winner does not boast, and a good loser says well done. Winning is not only about the result; it is also about how you treat other people.
fact: Winner is a noun. Its plural is winners.
fact: «Winner» means a person, team or animal that wins a game, race, competition or prize.
fact: «Winner» can also mean something very successful or popular.
fact: In football, «the winning goal» is the goal that wins the match.
fact: A good winner does not boast, and a good loser congratulates the winner.
exercise: «The winner of the race crossed the line first.» What does winner mean here? | The last runner to finish | A referee with a whistle | A sweet treat given to every runner | *A person who wins the race
exercise: Ella says, «This cake recipe is a winner.» What does she mean? | It won a prize at the shop | *It is a very successful, popular recipe | It is a recipe for a sports game | It is the longest recipe in the book
exercise: What is the best way for a good winner to behave? | Shout at the losers | Refuse to shake hands | Rub it in and boast loudly | *Be happy without boasting
test: «In the quiz, the winner is the team with the most points.» What is the winner here? | The quiz master | The team with the fewest points | The team that came last | *The team with the most points
test: In football, what is «the winning goal»? | A goal scored at the start of the game | *The goal that wins the match | A goal that is disallowed by the referee | The first goal of the season
exam: Which sentence uses winner to mean something very popular or successful? | «The winner of the race has the smallest time.» | *«This new game is a real winner, and everyone wants a copy.» | «The winner stood on the podium, holding up the gold cup.»
